---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import firesmoke from '../images/firesmoke.webp';
import skowint from '../images/skowint.webp';
import boots from '../images/boots.webp';
import nordsnow from '../images/nordsnow.webp';
---

<Layout title="The Story - Rewild" description="The story of Rewild, and the philosophy behind it.">

  <!-- Navigation -->
  <Nav />

  <!-- Story -->
  <section class="bg-white pt-36 pb-24 md:pt-44 md:pb-36">
    <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-6 md:px-12">
      <div class="grid gap-14 md:grid-cols-2 md:gap-24">
        <div class="md:order-1 md:sticky md:top-32 self-start">
          <Image
            src={firesmoke}
            alt="Fire smoke"
            widths={[480, 720, 1080]}
            sizes="(min-width: 768px) 480px, calc(100vw - 48px)"
            class="w-full h-auto aspect-[4/5] object-cover object-center"
            loading="lazy"
          />
        </div>
        <div class="md:order-2">
          <h1 class="font-display font-bold text-3xl md:text-4xl text-forest mb-6 md:mb-10 leading-tight">
            The Story of Rewild
          </h1>
          <div class="space-y-6 text-forest font-light leading-relaxed text-[1.08rem]">
            <p>
              While rebuilding my life from a crisis, I found myself in a place I no longer had the capacity to be in. The intensity of challenges left me injured and burnt out.
            </p>
            <p>
              My chest was in constant physical pain from accumulated stress and emotions. I had a knee and shoulder injury that wouldn't heal. I felt depressed, trapped and isolated, seeing no apparent solution to my life situation.
            </p>
            <p>
              My instincts were telling me to get out. To move it out of my system.
            </p>
            <p>
              I began to walk up local mountains, as if to grasp for air while suffocating. At first gently, then it intensified. Straight from work, in all weather, every season.
            </p>
            <Image
              src={nordsnow}
              alt="Snowy mountain trail"
              widths={[480, 720, 1080, 1440, 1800]}
              sizes="calc(100vw - 48px)"
              class="md:hidden w-full h-auto aspect-[3/2] object-cover object-center"
              loading="lazy"
            />
            <p>
              I welcomed the elements as a gateway into presence. Alone and far from anyone. Sometimes hiking up in deep snow.
            </p>
            <p>
              My lungs working hard to keep me moving. With each breath, tensions releasing. Every part of my body coming online. Every cell filling with life.
            </p>
            <p>
              Immersing in nature with all of my senses. Nostrils sticking from the cold air, picking up the citrusy scent of spruce needles. Reminding me of life all around.
            </p>
            <p>
              The soft hiss of snow crystals flowing from trees. Onto the ground covered in glitter.
            </p>
            <Image
              src={skowint}
              alt="Footprints in deep snow on a mountain ridge at sunset"
              widths={[480, 720, 1080, 1440, 1800]}
              sizes="calc((100vw - 48px) * 1.19)"
              class="md:hidden w-full h-auto aspect-[3/2] object-cover object-center"
              loading="lazy"
            />
            <p>
              I felt overwhelmed by gratitude. For witnessing this spectacle. For feeling at home here. And inside of myself.
            </p>
            <p>
              Where spaces inhabited by stress were cleared. Then re-filled with pure life. Again and again, and again...
            </p>
            <p>
              Even though physically challenging, the trips became addictive. Resistance to doing this seemingly hard thing disappeared. Leaving me with joy, peace and deep appreciation of being alive. In awe of the incredible beauty of nature.
            </p>
            <Image
              src={boots}
              alt="Boots resting in the snow at sunset"
              widths={[480, 720, 1080, 1400]}
              sizes="calc(100vw - 48px)"
              class="md:hidden w-full h-auto aspect-[2/3] object-cover object-center"
              loading="lazy"
            />
            <p>
              The effects lingered. My capacity to deal with stress in daily life expanded. My perspective shifted. Resilience increased.
            </p>
            <p>
              My body felt strong and capable. My knee and shoulder healed.
            </p>
            <p>
              Even my life began to change. I was able to buy a house. I started to pursue a path aligned with my inner compass. I found myself in a loving relationship that I forgot I always wanted.
            </p>
            <p>
              Stress was no longer my baseline. Survival mode gave way to creativity and a sense of freedom. It remains to this day.
            </p>
            <p>
              The transformation wildly inspired me to share these tools with others. So they can feel the same relief and strength in their own lives.
            </p>
            <p>
              These trips turned out to be the very first, organic form of the <a href="/#events" class="font-semibold underline decoration-forest/40 hover:decoration-forest transition-colors duration-200">Evening Reset</a>. Now more refined, accessible, and constantly evolving.
            </p>
            <p>
              With you.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Footer -->
  <Footer />

</Layout>
